, and two families of storm petrels. Formerly called Tubinares and still called tubenoses in English, Procellariiformes are often referred to collectively as the petrels, a term that has been applied to all members of the order, or more commonly all the families except the albatrosses.","revisionId":1371062746,"title":"Procellariiformes","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procellariiformes","wikidataId":"Q21685"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"logrunners","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"logrunner","source":"The Paleobiology Database"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Orthonychidae","confidence":94,"rank":"family","scientificName":"Orthonychidae","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":9609},"ottId":488749,"rank":"family","scientificName":"Orthonychidae","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Orthonychidae is a clade of passerine birds endemic to Australia and New Guinea. It encompasses the genus Orthonyx, (from Ancient Greek ὀρθός (orthós), meaning \"straight\", and ὄνῠξ (ónŭx), meaning \"claw\") including the logrunners and the chowchilla.","revisionId":1369647095,"title":"Orthonychidae","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthonychidae","wikidataId":"Q782767"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Barbary Macaque","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Barbary Ape","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Macaca sylvanus","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Macaca sylvanus (Linnaeus, 1758)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2436618},"ottId":689645,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Macaca sylvanus","synonyms":["Inuus ecaudatus","Macaco sylvanus","Pithecus pygmaeus","Simia inuus","Simia pithecus","Simia sylvanus"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Barbary macaque (Macaca sylvanus) is a macaque species native to the Atlas Mountains of Morocco, Algeria and Tunisia, along with a small introduced population in Gibraltar. It is the type species of the genus Macaca.","revisionId":137632697